@startuml
title SEQ-02 - Token Refresh and GotIt Product Authentication
autonumber
actor User
boundary Client
control Core
control GotIt as "GotIt Backend"
database CoreDB as "core"

User -> Client: Open protected screen / invoke action
alt Access token valid beyond skew
  Client -> GotIt: Product request\nAuthorization: Bearer JWT
else Access missing or near expiry
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/refresh\n{refreshToken}
  Core -> CoreDB: SELECT session FOR UPDATE
  Core -> Core: Validate application/user/hash/expiry/revocation
  break Invalid or replayed refresh
    Core --> Client: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN
    Client -> Client: Clear tokens
    Client --> User: Sign-in required
  end
  critical Rotate secret
    Core -> CoreDB: Replace refresh hash + last_used_at
    Core -> Core: Sign new access JWT
  end
  Core --> Client: rotated tokens
  Client -> GotIt: Product request with new JWT
end
GotIt -> Core: GET /auth/me\nX-Application-Key: gotit\nBearer same JWT
Core -> Core: Verify signature, issuer, audience, app and claims
Core -> CoreDB: Load current user status and role
alt Valid active identity
  Core --> GotIt: trusted user/application/role
  GotIt -> GotIt: Build gotitAuth scope
  GotIt -> GotIt: Entitlement lookup when route requires it
  GotIt --> Client: Product response
else Invalid/disabled/wrong application
  Core --> GotIt: 401/403
  GotIt --> Client: fail closed
else Core unavailable
  GotIt --> Client: 503 CORE_AUTH_UNAVAILABLE
end
note over Client,GotIt
Client never supplies application_user_id as authority.
GotIt does not bypass Core when Core is unavailable.
end note
@enduml

